instantnoodle-xnu
=================

This repository builds on:

- HackiOS by OOSEX GANG (https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel and its user space), which brought
  Apple's XNU kernel and the iOS 16.5 user space to the POCO X5 Pro (redwood) and QEMU.
- haxi0/iphont-xnu-kernel and haxi0/iphont-xnu-userland, the OnePlus 8 (instantnoodle) port this work started from.
- Project Silicium / Mu-Silicium (https://github.com/Project-Silicium/Mu-Silicium), the UEFI the phone boots
  through (uefi/).
- dekefake/hackios-op8pro (https://github.com/dekefake/hackios-op8pro), the HackiOS port to the OnePlus 8 Pro. The
  cellular path here (tools/nf/cell: the modem driver, its MHI host and network interface, and the call additions to
  the audio drivers) is ported from its commit e5631cd, under the same Apple Public Source License 2.0. The ported
  files carry its text and name it at their head; tools/nf/cell/fetch-ref.sh fetches the unmodified originals.

Apple, iOS and XNU are trademarks of Apple Inc. The XNU sources and the patches to them are under the Apple Public
Source License 2.0 (LICENSE). This project is not affiliated with, authorised or endorsed by Apple Inc., OnePlus or
Qualcomm.

Not included: no Apple files (no IPSW contents, no dyld shared cache, no Apple binaries or keys), no device dumps,
no logs. The build scripts under ios165/ and userland/ take what they need from the user's own IPSW download, and
the camera and Wi-Fi firmware from the user's own phone, at build time.

Included third-party binaries, as in the upstream repositories:

- uefi/files/Binaries/ and prebuilt/uefi/: UEFI driver binaries extracted from the phones' boot firmware (xbl) with
  UEFIReader, as Project Silicium distributes them for each device. They remain the property of their owners
  (Qualcomm and the device makers); see the README files next to them.
- prebuilt/: the kernel, the EFI loader and the user-space programs built from this repository's own sources.
- uefi/files/Resources/DTBs/: device trees taken from the phones.
- wifi/: the Linux ath11k/mac80211 sources it builds on keep their own licenses (GPL-2.0 / ISC), as marked in the
  files.
